{"type":"standard","title":"Western Niger Fulfulde","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Western Niger Fulfulde</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q12952430","titles":{"canonical":"Western_Niger_Fulfulde","normalized":"Western Niger Fulfulde","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Western Niger Fulfulde</span></span>"},"pageid":75510223,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Peul_du_Niger_occidental_%28fuh%29.svg/330px-Peul_du_Niger_occidental_%28fuh%29.svg.png","width":330,"height":250},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Peul_du_Niger_occidental_%28fuh%29.svg/1280px-Peul_du_Niger_occidental_%28fuh%29.svg.png","width":1028,"height":780},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1326985578","tid":"ca6aa7b8-d6ef-11f0-b912-d58b0d745de1","timestamp":"2025-12-12T00:16:23Z","description":"Variety of the Fula language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Niger_Fulfulde","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Niger_Fulfulde?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Niger_Fulfulde?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Western_Niger_Fulfulde"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Niger_Fulfulde","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Western_Niger_Fulfulde","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Niger_Fulfulde?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Western_Niger_Fulfulde"}},"extract":"Western Niger Fulfulde, also known as Gorgal Niiser Fulfulde is a variety of the Fula language, spoken mainly in Niger, and Burkina Faso, as well as by a small number of speakers in Benin by 3 million people. It has SOV word order and is closely related to other varieties of Fula spoken in Niger.","extract_html":"<p><b>Western Niger Fulfulde</b>, also known as <b>Gorgal Niiser Fulfulde</b> is a variety of the Fula language, spoken mainly in Niger, and Burkina Faso, as well as by a small number of speakers in Benin by 3 million people. It has SOV word order and is closely related to other varieties of Fula spoken in Niger.</p>"}